.TH OPENSLIDE\-WRITE\-TILES 1 2026-07-13 "OpenSlide @SUFFIXED_VERSION@" "User Commands"

.mso www.tmac

.SH NAME
openslide\-write\-tiles \- Experimental - Output the tiles of a virtual slide to a directory in their original encoding format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR "openslide\-write\-tiles " [ \-\-help "] [" \-\-version ]
.I slide-file level width height output-directory

.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the tiles the specified
.I level
of a virtual slide to files in their original encoding.
.I width
and
.I height
are pixel dimensions in the specified
.IR level .

The dimensions of each level of a slide can be obtained with
.BR openslide\-show\-properties (1).

-I output
directory where the tiles are written

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display usage summary.

.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version and copyright information.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.B openslide\-write\-tiles
returns 0 on success, 1 if an error occurred,
or 2 if the arguments are invalid.

.SH NOTES
.B openslide\-write\-tiles
is experimental and output should be examined with care

